OSKit INET TCP — outbound emit (header build + options + xmit)
================================================================

Same-module sibling of `tcp.lsysl`. Owns `inet_tcp_emit` — the
single funnel for every outbound TCP segment, which composes the
Ethernet/IP framing, the TCP header (including SYN options /
post-SYN Timestamps / SACK blocks), the segment-window
mathematics, and finally the NIC hand-off. Also keeps
`inet_tcp_eff_mss` (PMTU-driven payload cap) next to its only
caller.

    module oskit.servers

    import oskit.services.{monotonic_ms}
    import std.net.{ipv4, pkt_write_mac, pkt_write_u16, pkt_write_ipv4,
        ETHERTYPE_IPV4, IP_PROTO_TCP, ipv4_octet, net_checksum}


PMTU-driven effective MSS (RFC 1191 §5). The send-side payload
cap is `pmtu - IP(20) - TCP(<=40 with options)`. Slix's drain
path picks the segment size before knowing the exact option
shape — Timestamps + SACK can grow the header to 36 or 40
bytes — so we conservatively reserve 40 bytes for the TCP
header. Over-conservative just means slightly smaller
segments on the wire, never a frame-too-big rejection inside
`inet_tcp_emit`. Loopback destinations hit the same lookup;
the default-MTU miss returns 1500 so the existing TCP_MAX_SEG
ceiling continues to dominate when the cache hasn't learned
anything.

A floor of 1 byte prevents a degenerate cap from stalling the
connection — if a peer reports an MTU below the architectural
minimum the cache clamps it to `INET_PMTU_MIN=296` anyway, so
this floor is belt-and-suspenders.

    inet_tcp_eff_mss(s: int) -> int
        val pmtu = inet_pmtu_get(tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip)
        var cap = pmtu - 20 - 40
        if cap < 1
            cap = 1
        cap

`inet_tcp_data_seg_emit_count` ticks whenever `inet_tcp_emit`
sends a segment carrying user payload (any non-zero
`payload_len`). Pure ACKs, retransmits with payload, SYN/FIN
without data, and the loopback fastpath all pass through —
the counter records data delivery as observed at the emit
seam, not the wire. Test scaffolding reads this counter
across a `send()` to assert the segment count matches what a
PMTU-clamped path would produce.

    var inet_tcp_data_seg_emit_count: int = 0


Build a single Ethernet + IPv4 + TCP frame for socket `s`. Payload
is `payload_len` bytes of send_buf starting at `payload_seq`
(relative to snd_una).

TCP options attached:

- Active SYN frames advertise MSS + SACK-permitted + Timestamps
  + Window-scale: 20 bytes of options, `hdr_bytes = 40`.
- SYN-ACK frames echo TS / WS only if the peer's SYN advertised
  them.  The exact layout follows from the include flags below.
- Post-handshake segments include a 12-byte TS block (2 NOPs +
  10-byte option) once TS has been negotiated, plus an optional
  SACK block when reorder slots are populated.
- All other segments carry no options — `hdr_bytes = 20`.

    inet_tcp_emit(s: int, flags: int, seq: u32,
                  payload_seq: u32, payload_len: int) -> int
        // Test-only ACK blackhole. When `ack_blackholed != 0`, drop
        // pure-ACK segments (ACK set, no payload, no SYN/FIN/RST).
        // SYN/FIN/RST still fly so the test can establish + tear
        // down the connection; only acknowledgements are silently
        // discarded, which on slix's synchronous loopback fastpath
        // is the only way to simulate "peer went dark" without
        // breaking handshake.
        if tcp_sockets[s].ack_blackholed != 0
            val pure_ack_mask = TCP_F_ACK
            val deny_mask = TCP_F_SYN | TCP_F_FIN | TCP_F_RST
            if (flags & deny_mask) == 0
                if (flags & pure_ack_mask) != 0
                    if payload_len == 0
                        return 0
        if inet_our_mac_known == 0
            return -1
        val is_loopback = inet_is_loopback_ip(tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip)
        var next_hop_mac: [6]byte
        if is_loopback != 0
            // Loopback never goes to the NIC; the eth header is
            // ignored on the inbound dispatch path so any MAC is
            // fine. Re-using `inet_our_mac` keeps construction
            // uniform with the wire path below.
            var mi = 0
            while mi < 6
                next_hop_mac[mi] = inet_our_mac[mi]
                mi += 1
        else
            if inet_resolve_mac(tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip, next_hop_mac) == 0
                // ARP request now in-flight.  Mark the slot so
                // `inet_arp_drain_pending` can re-emit when the
                // reply lands, instead of waiting an RTO.
                tcp_sockets[s].arp_pending = 1
                return -1
        val is_syn = (flags & TCP_F_SYN) != 0
        // Count SACK blocks we'd emit on this segment. SACK is
        // only ever attached to non-SYN ACKs once both sides
        // agreed on SACK-permitted at handshake.
        var sack_count = 0
        if is_syn == 0
            if (flags & TCP_F_ACK) != 0
                if tcp_sockets[s].sack_ok != 0
                    var ri = 0
                    while ri < TCP_REORDER_SLOTS
                        if tcp_sockets[s].reorder[ri].in_use != 0
                            if sack_count < TCP_MAX_SACK_BLOCKS
                                sack_count += 1
                        ri += 1
        // RFC 7323 negotiate-and-echo rules. Active SYN (no ACK
        // bit) advertises everything we support. SYN-ACK only
        // includes options the peer's SYN already opted into.
        // Post-handshake includes TS on every segment iff TS was
        // negotiated.
        var include_ts = 0
        var include_ws = 0
        if is_syn
            if (flags & TCP_F_ACK) == 0
                include_ts = 1
                include_ws = 1
            else
                if tcp_sockets[s].ts_ok != 0
                    include_ts = 1
                if tcp_sockets[s].rcv_wscale != 0
                    include_ws = 1
        else
            if tcp_sockets[s].ts_ok != 0
                include_ts = 1
        var hdr_bytes = 20
        if is_syn
            // MSS(4) + SACK_PERM(2) = 6, then variable trailers
            // chosen so the total stays 4-byte aligned.
            if include_ts != 0 && include_ws != 0
                hdr_bytes = 40
            else if include_ts != 0
                hdr_bytes = 36
            else if include_ws != 0
                hdr_bytes = 32
            else
                hdr_bytes = 28
        else
            if include_ts != 0
                hdr_bytes = 32
                if sack_count > 0
                    hdr_bytes = 32 + 4 + 8 * sack_count
            else if sack_count > 0
                hdr_bytes = 20 + 4 + 8 * sack_count
        var seg_len = hdr_bytes + payload_len
        if seg_len > 1460
            return -1
        if payload_len > 0
            inet_tcp_data_seg_emit_count += 1
        val fidx = inet_frame_alloc()
        val frame = inet_frame_buf(fidx)
        val total_len = 14 + 20 + seg_len
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 0, next_hop_mac)
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 6, inet_our_mac)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 12, ETHERTYPE_IPV4)
        frame[14] = 0x45
        frame[15] = 0
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 16, 20 + seg_len)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 18, 0)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 20, 0x4000)
        frame[22] = 64
        frame[23] = byte(IP_PROTO_TCP)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, 0)
        val our_ip = ipv4(INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B,
            INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 26,
            INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B, INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 30,
            ipv4_octet(tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip, 0),
            ipv4_octet(tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip, 1),
            ipv4_octet(tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip, 2),
            ipv4_octet(tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip, 3))
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, net_checksum(frame + 14, 20))
        val tcp_off = 34
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 0, tcp_sockets[s].local_port)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 2, tcp_sockets[s].remote_port)
        tcp_write_u32(frame, tcp_off + 4, seq)
        var ack_val: u32 = u32(0)
        if (flags & TCP_F_ACK) != 0
            ack_val = tcp_sockets[s].rcv_nxt
        tcp_write_u32(frame, tcp_off + 8, ack_val)
        val data_off_words = hdr_bytes / 4
        frame[tcp_off + 12] = byte((data_off_words << 4) & 0xf0)
        frame[tcp_off + 13] = byte(flags & 0xff)
        val stashed = inet_tcp_reorder_bytes(s)
        var rwnd = tcp_sockets[s].recv_buf_size - tcp_sockets[s].recv_len - stashed
        if rwnd < 0
            rwnd = 0
        // RFC 7323 §2.2: SYN segments advertise the unscaled
        // window field; non-SYN segments advertise (rwnd >>
        // rcv_wscale). When `rcv_wscale == 0` (no negotiation)
        // the shift is a no-op.
        var rwnd_field = rwnd
        if is_syn == 0
            rwnd_field = rwnd >> tcp_sockets[s].rcv_wscale
        if rwnd_field > 0xffff
            rwnd_field = 0xffff
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 14, rwnd_field)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 16, 0)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 18, 0)
        // Compute the values we'll write into the TS option.
        // tsval baked from a per-connection random offset so
        // the host kernel's tick count doesn't leak; tsecr
        // mirrors `ts_recent`, which is 0 on the initial active
        // SYN (peer hasn't advertised yet).
        val tsval = u32(monotonic_ms()) + tcp_sockets[s].ts_offset
        val tsecr = tcp_sockets[s].ts_recent
        if is_syn
            // MSS (RFC 793): kind=2 len=4 value=TCP_MSS_ADV
            frame[tcp_off + 20] = byte(TCP_OPT_MSS)
            frame[tcp_off + 21] = 4
            pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 22, TCP_MSS_ADV)
            // SACK-permitted (RFC 2018 §2): kind=4 len=2
            frame[tcp_off + 24] = byte(TCP_OPT_SACK_PERMITTED)
            frame[tcp_off + 25] = 2
            if include_ts != 0 && include_ws != 0
                // TS at +26..35, NOP at +36, WS at +37..39.
                frame[tcp_off + 26] = byte(TCP_OPT_TS)
                frame[tcp_off + 27] = 10
                tcp_write_u32(frame, tcp_off + 28, tsval)
                tcp_write_u32(frame, tcp_off + 32, tsecr)
                frame[tcp_off + 36] = byte(TCP_OPT_NOP)
                frame[tcp_off + 37] = byte(TCP_OPT_WSCALE)
                frame[tcp_off + 38] = 3
                frame[tcp_off + 39] = byte(TCP_RCV_WSCALE)
            else if include_ts != 0
                // TS at +26..35, already aligned.
                frame[tcp_off + 26] = byte(TCP_OPT_TS)
                frame[tcp_off + 27] = 10
                tcp_write_u32(frame, tcp_off + 28, tsval)
                tcp_write_u32(frame, tcp_off + 32, tsecr)
            else if include_ws != 0
                // 2 NOPs at +26..27, WS at +28..30, NOP at +31.
                frame[tcp_off + 26] = byte(TCP_OPT_NOP)
                frame[tcp_off + 27] = byte(TCP_OPT_NOP)
                frame[tcp_off + 28] = byte(TCP_OPT_WSCALE)
                frame[tcp_off + 29] = 3
                frame[tcp_off + 30] = byte(TCP_RCV_WSCALE)
                frame[tcp_off + 31] = byte(TCP_OPT_NOP)
            else
                // Pad to 4-byte alignment with NOPs (legacy layout).
                frame[tcp_off + 26] = byte(TCP_OPT_NOP)
                frame[tcp_off + 27] = byte(TCP_OPT_NOP)
        else
            var opts_cur = tcp_off + 20
            if include_ts != 0
                // 2 NOPs + TS option = 12 bytes, naturally aligned.
                frame[opts_cur] = byte(TCP_OPT_NOP)
                frame[opts_cur + 1] = byte(TCP_OPT_NOP)
                frame[opts_cur + 2] = byte(TCP_OPT_TS)
                frame[opts_cur + 3] = 10
                tcp_write_u32(frame, opts_cur + 4, tsval)
                tcp_write_u32(frame, opts_cur + 8, tsecr)
                opts_cur += 12
            if sack_count > 0
                // 2 NOPs prefix for alignment (Linux emits this
                // pattern too) — placing SACK at a 4-byte boundary.
                frame[opts_cur]     = byte(TCP_OPT_NOP)
                frame[opts_cur + 1] = byte(TCP_OPT_NOP)
                // SACK header: kind=5, len = 2 + 8 * nblocks.
                frame[opts_cur + 2] = byte(TCP_OPT_SACK)
                frame[opts_cur + 3] = byte(2 + 8 * sack_count)
                var out_off = opts_cur + 4
                var ri2 = 0
                var emitted = 0
                while ri2 < TCP_REORDER_SLOTS
                    if emitted < sack_count
                        if tcp_sockets[s].reorder[ri2].in_use != 0
                            val blk_left = tcp_sockets[s].reorder[ri2].seq
                            val blk_right = blk_left + u32(tcp_sockets[s].reorder[ri2].len)
                            tcp_write_u32(frame, out_off, blk_left)
                            tcp_write_u32(frame, out_off + 4, blk_right)
                            out_off += 8
                            emitted += 1
                    ri2 += 1
        if payload_len > 0
            val offset = int(i32(payload_seq - tcp_sockets[s].snd_una))
            var i = 0
            while i < payload_len
                frame[tcp_off + hdr_bytes + i] = tcp_sockets[s].send_buf_ptr[offset + i]
                i += 1
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 16,
            (~inet_l4_partial_sum(our_ip, tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip,
                IP_PROTO_TCP, frame, tcp_off, seg_len)) & 0xffff)
        if is_loopback != 0
            // Swap IP src/dst so the inbound dispatcher sees a
            // peer-shaped frame, then recompute IP and TCP
            // checksums against the new pseudo-header. The TCP
            // pseudo-header was originally `(our_ip, remote_ip)`;
            // on inbound it will be evaluated as `(src_from_frame,
            // our_ip)`, so swapping puts both into agreement.
            var sw = 0
            while sw < 4
                val tmp = frame[26 + sw]
                frame[26 + sw] = frame[30 + sw]
                frame[30 + sw] = tmp
                sw += 1
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, 0)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, net_checksum(frame + 14, 20))
            val src_in = ipv4(int(frame[26]) & 0xff, int(frame[27]) & 0xff,
                int(frame[28]) & 0xff, int(frame[29]) & 0xff)
            val dst_in = ipv4(int(frame[30]) & 0xff, int(frame[31]) & 0xff,
                int(frame[32]) & 0xff, int(frame[33]) & 0xff)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 16, 0)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 16,
                (~inet_l4_partial_sum(src_in, dst_in,
                    IP_PROTO_TCP, frame, tcp_off, seg_len)) & 0xffff)
            inet_tcp_handle_segment(frame, total_len, 20)
            inet_frame_release(fidx)
            return 0
        inet_nic_send_packet(frame, total_len)
        inet_frame_release(fidx)
        0
